Sval: expose a wheel event's momentum and gesture start to chrome

The Workspace panel's swipe and the strip's wheel switch one Workspace for
each trackpad swipe. A DOM wheel event carries no phase: Gecko knows which
events are a pan gesture's start and which its momentum (PanGestureInput),
but WheelEvent exposes neither, chrome-only or not, no observer topic or
nsIDOMWindowUtils call reports them, and the platform events that mark a
touch and a lift (eWheelOperationStart and End) have no DOM name. The
swipe tracker's MozSwipeGesture events cover horizontal swipes only, where
the system's swipe-between-pages setting is on, so a vertical wheel over
the strip has no signal at all. Without one, a swipe begun while the last
one's momentum runs cannot be told from that momentum.

WidgetWheelEvent already carries mIsMomentum. This adds mIsGestureStart,
set on a PANGESTURE_START's wheel event, and exposes both on WheelEvent to
chrome only, with a sendWheelEvent flag so tests can synthesize a start.

